ithub.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The problem is that we have `deprecated` and `experimental` attributes, but not `obsolete`.\r\n\r\nObsoleting (as in keeping a method registered but it's no-op) doesn't make much sense in general. The only reason to do so is to avoid breaking ABI compatibility for GDExtension (which can make extensions using that method crash). But I think those can be handled by registering a compat method for GDExtension specifically using our dedicated framework for that.\r\n\r\nScripts would still break, but since the behavior breaks anyway, it's probably best this way so users notice and fix their code to remove usage of the obsoleted API.\r\n\r\n> Alternatively, we could keep the functionality, but still document it as deprecated.\r\n\r\nWe could, but that basically forces us to not only keep it but also implement it in `FileDialog` (which is what #111120 was doing), since the whole point of these series of changes is to unify the two classes' inheritance.","created_at":"2025-10-22T10:16:10Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T10:16:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111162#discussion_r2451467836","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111162","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2451467836"},"html":{"href":"ht